review_comments.body:
**Security: Symlink bypass — no filesystem-level resolution before bind-mount**

`validateHostPath` performs only string-based prefix matching after `filepath.Clean`. It never resolves symlinks on the actual filesystem. If any file or directory under an allowed prefix is a symbolic link pointing to a sensitive location outside the prefix (`/data/shared/escape -> /etc/passwd`), the bind mount will expose that location.

**Suggested fix:** After the string-based check passes, resolve with `filepath.EvalSymlinks` and verify the resolved path also falls under an allowed prefix:

```go
func validateHostPath(hostPath string) (string, error) {
    allowedPrefixes := config.GetAllowedHostMountPrefixes()
    cleaned := filepath.Clean(hostPath)
    resolved, err := filepath.EvalSymlinks(cleaned)
    if err != nil {
        // Path doesn't exist yet — that's OK for bind mounts; validate the string path
        resolved = cleaned
    }
    for _, prefix := range allowedPrefixes {
        cleanedWithSlash := cleaned + "/"
        resolvedWithSlash := resolved + "/"
        if strings.HasPrefix(cleanedWithSlash, prefix) &&
           strings.HasPrefix(resolvedWithSlash, prefix) {
            return cleaned, nil
        }
    }
    return "", fmt.Errorf("hostPath %q is not within an allowed mount prefix", hostPath)
}
```

