**Critical: Missing trailing-slash and absolute-path enforcement in prefix validation**

The field comment says "Each entry must be an absolute path ending with `/`", but the validation only checks that the path is not root `/` after cleaning. It does **not** enforce that prefixes are absolute or end with `/`.

**Exploit scenario:** If an operator configures `allowed_host_mount_prefixes: ["/data/shared"]` (no trailing slash), then `strings.HasPrefix("/data/shared_evil/", "/data/shared")` returns `true`, incorrectly allowing paths like `/data/shared_evil/` that are not under the intended directory.

Suggested fix — add validation for both conditions:
```go
for _, p := range cfg.ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes {
    cleaned := filepath.Clean(p)
    if cleaned == "/" {
        return fmt.Errorf("allowed_host_mount_prefixes must not contain root path %q", p)
    }
    if !strings.HasPrefix(p, "/") {
        return fmt.Errorf("allowed_host_mount_prefixes entry %q must be an absolute path", p)
    }
    if !strings.HasSuffix(p, "/") {
        return fmt.Errorf("allowed_host_mount_prefixes entry %q must end with \"/\"", p)
    }
}
```

