review_comments.body:
**Medium: Error message leaks the full allowed-prefixes list to API clients**

This error is returned through gRPC to CubeAPI and ultimately reaches the end user as an HTTP 500 response (as the README itself shows). An attacker can probe the API to discover exactly which directories are trusted on every CubeMaster node.

**Performance note:** `GetAllowedHostMountPrefixes()` is also called inside the `for` loop, so it's re-queried on every iteration. Since the prefix list is immutable for the lifetime of the process (or config-reload cycle), resolve it once at the top of `validateHostPath`.

Suggested fix:
```go
func validateHostPath(hostPath string) error {
    cleaned := filepath.Clean(hostPath) + "/"
    prefixes := config.GetAllowedHostMountPrefixes()
    for _, prefix := range prefixes {
        if strings.HasPrefix(cleaned, prefix) {
            return nil
        }
    }
    return fmt.Errorf("hostPath %q is not in the allowed prefixes", hostPath)
}
```
If the full prefix list is needed for debugging, log it server-side via the structured logger instead.

