**High: `GetAllowedHostMountPrefixes` returns mutable reference to internal config slice**

When config is populated, this returns the backing slice of `config.ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes` directly. Any caller that mutates the returned slice (e.g. `prefixes[0] = "..."`) would corrupt the global config. The default branch correctly returns a fresh slice literal on line 1158, making the inconsistency visible.

Note also that there's no synchronization — if config hot-reload replaces `ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes` concurrently, this creates a data race. The `listenerMutex` nearby (line 1172) is unused for this access.

Suggested fix — return a defensive copy and add a read-lock comment:
```go
func GetAllowedHostMountPrefixes() []string {
    if c := cfg; c != nil && c.ExtraConf != nil && len(c.ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes) > 0 {
        out := make([]string, len(c.ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes))
        copy(out, c.ExtraConf.AllowedHostMountPrefixes)
        return out
    }
    return []string{"/data/shared/"}
}
```
Consider also using a package-level sentinel for the default to avoid the per-call heap allocation.

