review_comments.body:
**Partial PMU initialization risk** — This early return is hit on the *first* vCPU that lacks PMU. If vCPU 0 successfully completes `init_pmu(irq)` on line 883 but vCPU 1 has `pmu_enabled == false`, the function returns `Ok(false)` with vCPU 0's PMU already configured. The caller receives `Ok(false)` and cannot distinguish "no PMU at all" from "some vCPUs have PMU configured."

Recommendation: Add a pre-check loop that verifies *all* vCPUs have `pmu_enabled == true` before performing any PMU writes. This keeps the loop all-or-nothing:
```rust
for cpu in self.vcpus.iter() {
    if !cpu.lock().unwrap().pmu_enabled { return Ok(false); }
}
for cpu in self.vcpus.iter() { /* perform init_pmu */ }
```

