**Suggestion: check the sentinel value before the `Duration` multiplication**

When `TimeoutSeconds == -1`, the multiplication `time.Duration(-1) * time.Second` produces `-1s` before being immediately overwritten on the next line. While not a correctness issue (the product of `-1 * 1_000_000_000` fits comfortably in int64), reordering to check the sentinel first avoids the redundant operation and makes the intent clearer:

```go
if e.Meta.TimeoutSeconds == lifecycle.ImmediateExpireTimeoutSeconds {
    timeout = 0
} else {
    timeout = time.Duration(e.Meta.TimeoutSeconds) * time.Second
    if timeout <= 0 {
        timeout = s.o.DefaultIdleTimeout
    }
}
```

