**DNS policy flags may not be cleared on non-replace updates**

When `!replace && plan.dnsPolicyFlags == 0`, the call to `setDNSPolicyFlags` is skipped entirely. If an existing sandbox previously had DNS domains configured (non-zero flags) and receives an incremental `applyNetPolicy` (non-replace) with no domains, the old DNS policy flags would never be cleared.

While `applyNetPolicy` is currently only called from `AddTAPDevice` (new devices), it is an exported function. Consider either documenting this contract or using a safer guard:

```go
if replace || plan.dnsPolicyFlags != 0 {
    return setDNSPolicyFlags(ifindex, plan.dnsPolicyFlags)
}
```

