review_comments.body:
**SSRF bypass via IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses** — `validate_webhook_ip_literal` delegates to separate branches for IPv4 and IPv6 without checking IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses (`::ffff:x.x.x.x`). An attacker can encode a private IP (e.g., `10.0.0.1`, `169.254.169.254`) as `[::ffff:a00:1]` or `[::ffff:a9fe:a9fe]`. The IPv6 validator (`is_allowed_webhook_ipv6`) sees these as non-loopback, non-local, non-multicast addresses and returns `allowed = true`, bypassing SSRF protection entirely.

**Fix:** Check for embedded IPv4 before delegating to the IPv6 validator:

```rust
IpAddr::V6(ip) => {
    if let Some(ipv4) = ip.to_ipv4_mapped() {
        is_allowed_webhook_ipv4(ipv4)
    } else {
        is_allowed_webhook_ipv6(ip)
    }
}
```

