review_comments.body:
**JoinSet starvation under sustained load** — The biased `tokio::select!` prioritizes `rx.recv()` (line 154). When events arrive continuously, the `deliveries.join_next()` arm at line 184 is never polled because `rx.recv()` is always immediately ready. Completed delivery tasks accumulate in the `JoinSet` without being joined, causing unbounded memory growth over time.

**Fix:** Drain completed tasks non-blockingly after processing each event using `JoinSet::try_join_next()` before re-entering `select!`:

```rust
while let Ok(Some(result)) = deliveries.try_join_next() {
    if let Err(err) = result {
        warn!(error = %err, "HttpLogger: webhook delivery task failed");
    }
}
```

